
                                                          Date: Nov. 11th, 1996

 Dear WCOP8 User,

please find below some additional hints to get started with WCOP8 and how
to handle the example files provided on the disk.

I. This disk contains version 1.05 of WCOP8. In case you observe any kind of
  problems during installation of the software on your PC, or during operation
  of WCOP8, then please report these problems directly to 'KKD'. 

II. Receiving this disk you may ask for ONE official licence at 'KKD'. In order to 
  do so, please return the code #er written on the disk lable (4 digit code) 
  including your name and address-details to KKD. You will be also requested to
  provide the key-code to KKD in order to obtain the final valid licence code.
   This code is being displayed when opening WCOP8 and a valid licence
  code is not yet entered.

III. Once WCOP8 is established with a valid licence code it is fixed for ONE
  particular PC. So please carefully decide on which PC you want to run WCOP8.
  For later upgrades (revs) of WCOP8 there may be the chance to uninstall the s/w
  and port the licence onto another PC.

IV. You may distribute as many copies as you want. Installing WCOP8 on any new PC
  will open the chance to use it 30 days for free. Thereafter a lock will be activated
  and the user can only continue working with WCOP8 when purchasing a valid licence.
  Further details are explained in the user's manaul.

V. There are some additional COP800 coding examples included on the disk. Under:
   ... EXAMPL\ASMEXAMP you will find 4 files which can be assembled and linked with
   ASMCOP (version 4.6 and higher). The include files belonging to these files are
   placed under ... EXAMPL\ASMINCL. These files are suitable to be run as a project
   and allow to test all the advantages of WCOP8. The modules 'AD1.asm', 'PWM1.asm'
   and 'NM93C06.asm' are specific subroutines executing particular tasks.
    "AD1.asm" includes initialization and execution code for A/D in COP884EK devices.
   "PWM1.asm" includes lookup data and shows basically the way how to handle them.
   "NM93C06.asm" is an example for MicroWire Read/Write routines COP888x w/ EEPROM.

    Under ...EXAMPL\C-SOURCE there is a COP8C example file. All include files needed
   to compile this routine successfully are placed under ... EXAMPL\C_INCLUD 


